# 🚀 Time-Dilation Arena
**Real-Time Competitive Coding Spectator Sport**

## 🏟️ Overview
A full-stack platform where developers compete in live coding matches. Spectators can watch the logic unfold in real-time with sub-50ms latency, while a PostgreSQL backend tracks global ELO ratings.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** HTML5, CSS3 (Cyber-Glow UI), Socket.io Client
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express.js
- **Real-Time:** WebSockets (Socket.io)
- **Database:** PostgreSQL (Relational schema for Matches & Users)
- **Security:** Bcrypt (Password Hashing) & JWT (Authentication)

## ⚡ Key Features
- **Instant Broadcast:** Every keystroke is emitted via WebSockets to all connected spectators.
- **Global Leaderboard:** Live-updating standings pulled directly from the DB.
- **Secure Cockpit:** Only authenticated competitors can enter the Arena to broadcast code.